<title>CANADA: Shaw Communications Q4 net soars to $0.50.</title>
<headline>Shaw Communications Q4 net soars to $0.50.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended	 Three months ended</p>
<p>				 August 31		August 31</p>
<p>(000's except per</p>
<p>  share amounts)	     1996	1995	1996	1995</p>
<p>Total revenue from</p>
<p>  operations	     $584,430  $435,790  $148,946  $136,455</p>
<p> Net Income		  67,932    31,395    34,303     7,503</p>
<p>Cash flow per share:</p>
<p>Continuing</p>
<p>   operations		  1.70	1.57	0.52	0.39</p>
<p>Discontinued</p>
<p>   operations		  0.07	0.02	0.02	0.01</p>
<p>				   1.77	1.59	0.54	0.40</p>
<p>Earnings per share:</p>
<p>Before discontinued</p>
<p>   operations		  1.16	0.46	0.74	0.08</p>
<p>Discontinued</p>
<p>   operations	     ( 0.25)   ( 0.01)   ( 0.24)	   -</p>
<p>				   0.91	0.45	0.50	0.08</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is Shaw Communications Inc.  </p>
<p>The divestiture of non-strategic cable assets in Vancouver and Nova Scotia, completed during fiscal 1996, generated proceeds of approximately $163 million. This resulted in a pre-tax gain of $109 million or $67 million after-tax ($0.96 per share).</p>
<p>The loss on discontinued operations of $17.6 million in the fourth quarter includes provision for a potential after-tax loss of $14.6 million on the sale of the paging division.</p>
<p>Earnings were reduced by $0.03 per share due to a write-off in the CableSat investment.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
